'
' tkColorPicker -- PsColorPicker on SDL3 + SDL_ttf, a port of pkg/vendor/PsControls/PsColorPicker
' onto tkHost. A chromeless MODAL colour picker popup: tkColorPicker_DoModal puts it on screen,
' blocks until the user answers, and returns TRUE with the colour written back, or FALSE with the
' caller's variables untouched.
'
' THE SHAPE. Vendor's handle was the popup HWND itself, created hidden so the host could reach
' the setters first. Here the handle is a HIDDEN zero-size widget in the owner's tree that holds
' the state; the popup SURFACE (a TK_SURF_POPUP) is created by tkColorPicker_RunModal for each
' run and closed at its end -- Wayland cannot re-show an unmapped popup, and the state must
' outlive the surface so GetColor answers after the run. The content widget on the popup shares
' the state.
'
' WHAT IS UNCHANGED, by design: the layout (tab strip sized to its captions, a FIXED-height body,
' the preview / fields / OK bottom block), the matrix colour law, the Web table, the one edit
' buffer with select-all-on-entry, the field rules (digits only, three max, clamp on commit), the
' ColorChanged phases (BEGIN / MOVE / END, no END for an abandoned drag), the selection that
' follows the value, the keyboard (Esc cancels from anywhere, Enter commits a field or accepts,
' Tab walks the fields and WRAPS, arrows navigate the body), double-click-a-cell accepts, the OK
' press/slide-off gesture, click-Initial-reverts, silent setters, theme and pinning, the probes.
'
' WHAT CHANGED: the outside click is the router's popup dismissal (tkHost), so it cancels and
' the press is consumed, as vendor's loop did; the popup opts out of the router's other rule,
' closing when the application loses focus (bKeepOnFocusLoss), which vendor never had. Digits
' come from TKM_KEYDOWN, not WM_CHAR (a popup never owns the OS text input). The System tab is
' PsPlatform's frozen table of Windows' default system colours, overridable per entry -- SDL has
' no GetSysColor. Coordinates are OWNER window pixels, not screen pixels. See PORT.md.
#module "tkColorPicker"

#import "../tkHost" public
#import "../tkTheme" public
#import "../tkVScrollBar" public
using tkHost
using tkPaint
using tkTheme
using tkVScrollBar

